sc#1266836).\n- CVE-2026-31678: openvswitch: defer tunnel netdev_put to RCU release (bsc#1263562).\n- CVE-2026-31692: rtnetlink: add missing netlink_ns_capable() check for peer netns (bsc#1267741).\n- CVE-2026-31708: smb: client: fix OOB read in smb2_ioctl_query_info QUERY_INFO path (bsc#1264022).\n- CVE-2026-31709: smb: client: validate the whole DACL before rewriting it in cifsacl (bsc#1264024).\n- CVE-2026-43350: smb: client: require a full NFS mode SID before reading mode bits (bsc#1264985).\n- CVE-2026-64137: smb: client: require net admin for CIFS SWN netlink (bsc#1273966).\n- CVE-2026-72110: bpf,fork: wipe ->bpf_storage before bailouts that access it (bsc#1277357).\n- CVE-2026-72318: cifs: validate DFS referral string offsets (bsc#1275939).\n- CVE-2026-74334: RDMA/nldev: Fix locking when accessing mr->pd (bsc#1277095).\n- CVE-2026-74565: netfilter: nf_tables: make nft_object rhltable per table (bsc#1275568).\n- CVE-2026-74580: vhost: reset the vring metadata cache on vring reconfiguration (bsc#1277885).\n- CVE-2026-74746: netfilter: flowtable: publish GC-visible tuple last (bsc#1278101).\n- CVE-2026-80558: libceph: Avoid using invalid osd indices from primary_temp (bsc#1277485).\n- CVE-2026-80561: libceph: fix multiple unsafe decodes in decode_locker() (bsc#1277265).\n- CVE-2026-89530: svcrdma: Eliminate allocation of recv_ctxt objects in backchannel (bsc#1280920).\n- CVE-2026-89606: ecryptfs: reject too-small tag 70 packets (bsc#1280469).\n- CVE-2026-89607: ecryptfs: reject oversized encrypted_key_size in parse_tag_3_packet (bsc#1281792).\n- CVE-2026-89637: smb: client: fix UAF and buffer leak in cifs_check_trans2() for malformed secondary T2 (bsc#1280492).\n- CVE-2026-89650: ceph: bound num_export_targets array for mds info v2/v3 (bsc#1280417).\n- CVE-2026-89652: ceph: bound copied dentry name length in NFS export get_name (bsc#1280419).\n- CVE-2026-89653: ceph: reject export_targets ranks >= CEPH_MAX_MDS in mdsmap decode (bsc#1280401).\n- CVE-2026-89955: s390/vfio-ap: Fix NULL deref in status_show() during queue probe (bsc#1281400 bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-89956: s390/vfio-ap: Fix missing lock required to access list of ap_matrix_mdev objects (bsc#1281401\n  bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-89957: s390/vfio-ap: Fix hot-unplug skipped when last AP adapter or domain removed (bsc#1281405 bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-89958: s390/vfio-ap: Fix dereference matrix_mdev->kvm without checking for NULL (bsc#1281017 bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-89959: s390/vfio-ap: Fix control domain removal in vfio_ap_mdev_cfg_remove (bsc#1281219 bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-89960: s390/vfio-ap: fix stale pqap_hook pointer on error in vfio_ap_mdev_set_kvm() (bsc#1281217).\n- CVE-2026-90103: NFSv4.2: fix LAYOUTSTATS send buffer exhaustion (bsc#1281538).\n- CVE-2026-90148: NFSv4: Fix incorrect argument passed to nfs4_delete_lease() in nfs4_add_lease() (bsc#1281551).\n- CVE-2026-90227: nvme/ioctl: check SUBMIT_IO with nvme_cmd_allowed() (bsc#1281705).\n- CVE-2026-90393: bpf: Fix potential UAF in bpf_netns_link_update_prog (bsc#1282289).\n- CVE-2026-92507: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_dealloc_pd_user() (bsc#1281988).\n- CVE-2026-92508: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq() (bsc#1282034).\n- CVE-2026-92509: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in counter_release() (bsc#1282040).\n- CVE-2026-92510: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_destroy_srq_user() (bsc#1282041).\n- CVE-2026-92511: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_destroy_cq_user() (bsc#1282042).\n- CVE-2026-92512: RDMA/core: Fix use after free in ib_query_qp() (bsc#1281995).\n- CVE-2026-93054: uio: Fix stale info pointer in failed registration path (bsc#1282276).\n- CVE-2026-93207: SUNRPC: Zero rpc_gss_wire_cred at svcauth_gss_decode_credbody() entry (bsc#1282672).\n- CVE-2026-93238: s390/vfio-ap: fix potential use of uninitialized apm_filtered bitmap (bsc#1282689 bsc#1287662).\n- CVE-2026-93262: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush() (bsc#1283004).\n- CVE-2026-93817: perf: Fix addr_filter_ranges lifetime (bsc#1283017).\n- CVE-2026-97575: media: v4l2-ctrls: validate AV1 tile counts (bsc#1283337).\n- CVE-2026-97594: landlock: Fix use-after-free of the source's parent directory (bsc#1283487).\n- CVE-2026-97596: ipvs: reject invalid states in connection template sync records (bsc#1283941).\n- CVE-2026-97612: net: mpls: clear inner_protocol when the last label is popped (bsc#1283967).\n- CVE-2026-98017: net/sched: defer qdisc freeing after failed creation (bsc#1283021).\n- CVE-2026-98041: bpf: Don't predict JMP32 pointer vs zero comparisons (bsc#1284064).\n- CVE-2026-98171: smb: client: fix next_buffer UAF and NextCommand bounds in compound PDUs (bsc#1284419).\n- CVE-2026-98251: openvswitch: avoid reallocating confirmed conntrack labels (bsc#1284789).\n- CVE-2026-98258: posix-cpu-timers: Prevent freeing a timer which is queued on the expiry list (bsc#1284584).\n- CVE-2026-98264: ALSA: virtio: reset device before deleting virtqueues (bsc#1284363).\n- CVE-2026-98276: net: lock the socket in sock_gettstamp() (bsc#1284591).\n- CVE-2026-98282: powerpc/iommu: Fix the overflow validation in iommu_tce_check_ioba (bsc#1284360).\n- CVE-2026-98283: KVM: PPC: Book3S HV: fix use-after-free in kvmhv_emulate_tlbie_all_lpid() (bsc#1284595).\n- CVE-2026-98306: seg6: set IPSKB_L3SLAVE from IP6SKB_L3SLAVE on IPIP decapsulation (bsc#1284505).\n- CVE-2026-98364: xfrm: hold net_device reference under RCU in bundle creation (bsc#1284653).\n- CVE-2026-98368: esp: downgrade zerocopy managed frags before mutating skb frags (bsc#1284498).\n- CVE-2026-98370: xfrm: fix compat ALLOCSPI request use-after-free (bsc#1284744).\n- CVE-2026-98373: mm/hugetlb: preserve mremap address delta when skipping page tables (bsc#1284742).\n- CVE-2026-98374: tcp: fix use-after-free of retransmit_skb_hint in tcp_send_synack() (bsc#1284740).\n- CVE-2026-98417: net: xfrm: reject unrepresentable espintcp transport headers (bsc#1285674).\n- CVE-2026-98441: net/sched: act_ct: avoid modifying shared unconfirmed ct entry (bsc#1285952).\n- CVE-2026-98442: net/sched: act_ct: remove 'add_helper' dead code (bsc#1285961).\n- CVE-2026-98466: KVM: arm64: Transfer the hyp stack pages out of the host stage-2 (bsc#1286218).\n- CVE-2026-98491: net: openvswitch: conntrack: avoid modifying shared unconfirmed ct entry (bsc#1286838).\n- CVE-2026-98503: packet: use ubuf_info completion for TX_RING packets (bsc#1286020).\n- CVE-2026-98550: tipc: reject invalid and unexpected GRP_ACK_MSG to prevent bc_ackers underflow (bsc#1286437).\n- CVE-2026-98567: net: xps: reject an out of range traffic class (bsc#1286225).\n- CVE-2026-98857: ipvs: fix missing counter decrement in lblc (bsc#1286434).\n- CVE-2026-98863: KVM: x86: Re-pend GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES if getting said pages fails (bsc#1286257).\n- CVE-2026-98955: flow_dissector: avoid u16 truncation of skb->len when computing thoff (bsc#1287823).\n- CVE-2026-99095: drm/vc4: drain the hangcheck timer and works on V3D unbind (bsc#1288627).\n- CVE-2026-99109: smb: client: reject SetEA requests that do not fit the request buffer (bsc#1288737).\n\nThe following non security issues were fixed:\n\n- KVM: x86/mmu: Fix NX page unaccounting for TDP MMU pages (git-fixes).\n- KVM: x86: hyper-v: Clamp stimer deadline to avoid livelock (git-fixes).\n- KVM: x86: Take SRCU in kvm_zap_gfn_range() (git-fixes).\n- KVM: x86: Zero reserved synic flags when delivering message to avoid stack leak (git-fixes).\n- mm, vmscan: flush tlb before large folio is freed (bsc#1250656).\n- mm/gup: fix out-of-bounds write for nr_pages == 0 in GUP-fast (git-fixes).\n- mm/hugetlb: fix use-after-free of a new anon folio (git-fixes).\n- mm/mmu_notifier: set ->mm only after mmgrab() (git-fixes).\n- mm: memcontrol: fix NULL pointer deref and UAF from high_work_func() on dying memcg (git-fixes).\n- RDMA/core: Add rdma_restrack_begin/abort/commit_del() operations (git-fixes).\n- Revert 'mkspec: Exclude rt flavor from kernel-syms dependencies (bsc#1244337).\n- Revert 'rpm/mkspec: Fix missing kernel-syms-rt creation' (bsc#1244337).\n- s390/cpum_cf: Check session mask before cpu offline (bsc#1289558).\n- s390/ism: Zerorize dmb at allocation (bsc#1288232).\n- s390/smp: Remove conditional emergency signal order code (bsc#1287660).\n- s390/vfio-ap: Fix required lock not held during update of ap_matrix_mdev object (bsc#1287662).\n- s390/vfio-ap: Fix stale do_remove flag across iterations in vfio_ap_mdev_cfg_remove (bsc#1287662).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-default&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.4.0-150600.23.146.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-livepatch":"6.4.0-150600.23.146.1","kernel-default-livepatch-devel":"6.4.0-150600.23.146.1","kernel-livepatch-6_4_0-150600_23_146-default":"1-150600.13.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5369-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6_Update_34","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6_Update_34&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1-150600.13.3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-livepatch":"6.4.0-150600.23.146.1","kernel-default-livepatch-devel":"6.4.0-150600.23.146.1","kernel-livepatch-6_4_0-150600_23_146-default":"1-150600.13.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5369-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Availability Extension 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-default&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Availability%20Extension%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"t